# Deploy to firmshake-dev

After completing user-requested changes that affect the running app, deploy to **firmshake-dev** (devo) without waiting to be asked again. Do **not** deploy half-baked prod until `firmshake-prod` exists and CI secrets are ready. Dual-stack details: `docs/devo-prod-stacks.md`.

## Web app (this repo)

When frontend, Firestore rules, or hosting config change:

```bash
npm run deploy:hosting
# same as: npm run deploy:hosting:devo
```

If only Firestore rules changed:

```bash
npm run firebase:deploy-rules
```

- **Hosting URL:** https://firmshake-dev.web.app
- **Firebase project:** `firmshake-dev` (alias `devo`)
- Build uses `.env.local` locally; CI uses GitHub Environment `devo` secrets.
- Prod hosting: `npm run deploy:hosting:prod` only with prod `VITE_*` baked in.

## API (`firmshake-api` sibling repo)

When API code or Cloud Run env changes:

```bash
cd ../firmshake-api && bash scripts/deploy-staging.sh
# alias: bash scripts/deploy-devo.sh
```

- **API URL:** https://firmshake-api-staging-858269838319.us-central1.run.app
- Prod: `bash scripts/deploy-prod.sh` (us-east1) after project scaffolding.

## When to skip deploy

- Question-only or review-only tasks with no code changes
- User explicitly says not to deploy
- Dual-stack scaffolding / docs-only with no user-visible UI change
- Deploy fails — report the error; do not silently skip

## After deploy

Tell the user what was deployed and the URL(s).
